Where this code runs
--------------------
It runs RIPE Atlas probe 1018212:

  https://atlas.ripe.net/probes/1018212/

Each version deployed to that probe is tagged here (enodia-<NNNN>). The
current one is enodia-0028 (c8fbb6a), running since 2026-10-14 16:21 UTC.
This branch and its tags are the Corresponding Source for anyone who
interacts with the probe over the network (AGPL-3.0, section 13).

What changed
------------
0001-0005 make the probe fit to run as a system service. 0006-0028 bring
its behaviour on the wire in line with RIPE NCC's reference software probe
(ripe-atlas-software-probe, firmware 5130). Each commit message explains
the difference and cites the reference source it follows.

  0001  deps: refresh Cargo.lock and drop the unused hickory-client
  0002  controller: use russh's default key exchange (no group1-sha1)
  0003  registration: RIPE's reg-05/reg-06.prod servers
  0004  probe key: never replace an unreadable key; write it 0600
  0005  unit: a syscall filter systemd honours; a readable config
  0006  probe: send the address report (msm 9104) itself every 180 s
  0007  results: a failed upload keeps its telemetry lines
  0008  results: back off after an HTTP 429
  0009  results: a 429 is not a failed attempt; only age drops results
  0010  scheduler: run each measurement on its CRONLINE slot
  0011  controller: keep the registration across restarts; obey
        REREGISTER, WAIT and REFUSED
  0012  results: lts as the reference keeps it
  0013  results: status lines on the reference's cadence
  0014  results: traceroute, TLS and NTP results carry their real lts
  0015  ntp: evntp as of firmware 5130; report fw 5130
  0016  http: report like evhttpget, with the stored headers
  0017  controller: start registration at a random server
  0018  telnet: one OK per request, as the reference's telnetd answers
  0019  rptaddrs: the 9104 report byte for byte as rptaddrs.c writes it
  0020  uploads: post on the controller's httppost slots; one-offs on
        their own (&SRC=oneoff); httppost's header order
  0021  dns: evtdig as firmware 5130 asks and reports
  0022  tls: evsslgetcert as sslgetcert.c, recording any certificate
  0023  traceroute: evtraceroute's probes and reply matching; IPv6 UDP
        traces end at the target
  0024  ping: -s is the data after the ICMP header (32 bytes by
        default); target names, ttr and the replies' ttl
  0025  scheduler: crontab lines as eperd keeps them, one per line,
        not one per measurement id; a re-sent line keeps its slot
  0026  timing: a timer more than 10 s off is skipped with eperd's 9807
        record; no blocking name lookups; NTP matched as evntp; sends
        stamped right before the syscall (never deployed on its own:
        0027 includes it)
  0027  runtimes: measurements on their own threads at full priority,
        everything else on a background thread at lower priority;
        logging never blocks; SSH keepalive as the reference's ssh;
        start times spread within the second as eperd does; kernel
        receive timestamps as an option, off by default
  0028  the review lows and CON_KEEP_BROKEN: a KEEP the controller
        answers sends the probe back to register, as the reference
        does; the SSH login is time-bounded; https fetched as
        httpget fetches it, with its one timer, --timeout and --sni;
        NTP's busy check; perd's rules for crons/main; eperd's 9807
        waittime; SCHED_IDLE for background threads as an option,
        off by default (an earlier build of 0028, 56cd774, ran
        14:52-14:56 UTC on 2026-10-14 and was rolled back)

Upstream
--------
These changes are being offered to upstream as small pull requests, one
per bug. Until they are merged, this branch is the version that runs.
